  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "Here is what I found in your account. Two card payments to TechMart Online are settled, both for EUR 240.00:\n\n- **TX-0402**, 14 July 2026\n- **TX-0401**, 20 July 2026\n\nBoth are outgoing card payments on ACC-1005. Because the amounts and merchant match, the later payment (TX-0401) looks like a duplicate of the earlier one. That points more toward a **duplicate_charge** reason than the service_not_rendered code in my earlier notes, unless the goods or service were not delivered for one of them.\n\nTo move forward:\n\n1. **Tell me which transaction to dispute** (TX-0401 or TX-0402) and **which reason applies**: duplicate charge, or service not rendered.\n2. I will **check eligibility** for that transaction and reason before anything is filed. If it is not eligible, I will tell you why and I will not open the dispute.\n3. If it is eligible, I will **summarise the dispute** (transaction, amount, reason) and open it only after you explicitly confirm.\n\nI have not checked the dispute deadline with a tool yet, so I can't say how",
